---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { contact } from '../config';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility"
  kicker="Accessibility"
  description="PlayRun's accessibility statement: the site aims at WCAG 2.1 AA, is tested with axe and Playwright on every push, and how to report a problem."
  lead="I want everyone to be able to read this site and get in touch, whatever they use to browse it."
>
  <section class="row">
    <h2>What I aim for</h2>
    <p>
      The site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA. Text contrast meets AA on
      every field of colour, every image has a text alternative, every control has a name, and the whole site works
      with a keyboard alone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>How I test it</h2>
    <p>
      A Playwright suite runs against every push before the site can deploy. It includes an axe-core scan of every page
      at WCAG 2.1 A and AA, a check that each page has one main heading in the right order, that images carry
      alternative text, that keyboard focus is visible, and that nothing scrolls sideways on a phone. A failing check
      stops the deploy. The Quality page lists every test by name.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Motion and the games</h2>
    <p>
      The runner, the bug hunt and the achievement pop-ups are optional. If your system asks for reduced motion they
      are off and nothing on the site moves on its own. You can also switch them off with the Games button in the HUD
      bar. The page underneath never depends on them: the bugs are real buttons, and every pop-up is announced politely
      and never blocks what you are reading.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Pixel type</h2>
    <p>
      Headings, labels and figures are set in Pixel Operator, a pixel typeface, at sizes where it stays crisp. Running
      text is set in Montserrat at 16 pixels or more. If you zoom the page to 200% everything reflows without sideways
      scrolling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>What might still be wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Automated checks catch a lot but not everything. I have not yet had the site reviewed by people who use screen
      readers or switch access every day. If something does not work for you, I would like to know.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> with the page, what you were trying to do and what
      you use to browse. I read every message and fix what I can.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
